🚗 Smart Parking Assistance System using STM32 (Ultrasonic + Buzzer)
📌 Overview

This project implements a Smart Contactless Parking Assistance System using an STM32 microcontroller and an ultrasonic sensor. The system detects obstacles in real time and provides feedback through a buzzer with varying beep patterns based on distance, helping drivers park safely without physical contact.

🎯 Features
Real-time distance measurement
Ultrasonic sensor interfacing
Distance-based buzzer alert system
Dynamic beep frequency control
Low-cost and efficient design
🧠 Working Principle

The ultrasonic sensor emits sound waves and measures the time taken for the echo to return after hitting an obstacle. The STM32 calculates the distance based on this time. Depending on how close the object is, the buzzer produces different alert patterns, indicating proximity to the driver.

🔧 Hardware Used
STM32 (e.g., STM32F4 series / Trainer Kit)
Ultrasonic Sensor (HC-SR04)
Buzzer
Connecting wires
🔌 Pin Configuration
Component	Pin
Trigger (TRIG)	PB5
Echo (ECHO)	PA8
Buzzer	PA7
⚙️ Software Configuration
IDE: STM32CubeIDE
Language: C (HAL Drivers)
Timing: DWT-based microsecond delay
Measurement: Time-of-flight calculation
📊 Output Behavior
Distance Range	Buzzer Behavior
< 5 cm	Continuous ON
5 – 20 cm	Fast beeping
20 – 30 cm	Slow beeping
> 30 cm	OFF
🚀 How It Works
STM32 sends a trigger pulse to ultrasonic sensor
Sensor emits ultrasonic waves
Echo signal returns after hitting obstacle
STM32 measures echo duration using precise timing
Distance is calculated using sound velocity
Buzzer alert is generated based on distance range
▶️ How to Run
Open project in STM32CubeIDE
Build the project
Connect STM32 via ST-Link/USB
Flash the code
Place an object in front of the sensor
Observe buzzer alert changes with distance
⚠️ Notes
Ensure proper power supply to ultrasonic sensor
Avoid soft surfaces (may absorb sound waves)
Maintain correct sensor alignment
DWT must be enabled for accurate timing
Valid measurement range: 2 cm to 400 cm
